Now the landscape CSS. Replace the current media block:

```
@media (pointer: coarse) and (max-height: 520px) {
  .minimap-panel { display: none; }
  .hud-bottom { bottom: 10px; }
  .touch-controls {
    left: auto; right: 14px; bottom: 14px; width: auto; gap: 16px;
  }
  .touch-controls button { width: 58px; height: 58px; }
  .tap-gas { width: 66px !important; height: 66px !important; }
}
```

New:
```
@media (pointer: coarse) and (max-height: 520px) {
  .minimap-panel { display: none; }
  /* Compact centre gauge leaves both bottom corners free for thumbs. */
  .hud-bottom { left: 50%; right: auto; bottom: 6px; transform: translateX(-50%); }
  .speedo { width: 170px; height: 96px; padding: 6px; background: rgba(10,12,16,.55); }
  .speedo-arc { left: 8px; top: 8px; width: 150px; height: 84px; }
  .speedo-readout { left: 28px; top: 34px; width: 110px; }
  .speedo-readout strong { font-size: 36px; }
  .speedo-readout .mono { margin-top: 2px; font-size: 6px; }
  .gear-box { right: 8px; bottom: 8px; }
  .gear-box strong { font-size: 15px; }
  .throttle-strip { display: none; }
  .touch-controls {
    left: 12px; right: 12px; bottom: 14px; width: auto;
    justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px;
  }
  .touch-controls button { width: 58px; height: 58px; }
  .tap-gas { width: 66px !important; height: 66px !important; }
}
```
But note the mobile media (max-width 760?) sets `.speedo` 190 and touch controls display none? The landscape width 844 > 760, so base styles apply. At width ≤760 and height ≤520 (e.g. 700x390), the max-width 760 media sets speedo 190/105 and the new block overrides to 170/96; selector order: the new block comes after, so it wins for equal specificity. `.speedo` specificity equal, later wins. Good.

Also `.touch-controls` base display is none; `(pointer: coarse)` block sets display flex. The new landscape block doesn't set display, so okay.

One more: `.touch-steer` and `.touch-pedals` flex with gap; fine.

Will the speedo centered overlap with touch buttons at widths < 560? At 390 width in portrait, max-height >520, so not applied. For 600x400 landscape: speedo width 170 centered x 215-385, touch steer x 12-130 (two 58 buttons + gap 10 = 126), pedals x ~468-588. No overlap. Good. At 480x320: speedo x 155-325, pedals from 354, buttons width 58... 480-12-66 = 402 for gas; pedals two buttons 58+66+10 = 134 → x 334-468. Speedo ends 325, so 9px gap. Tight but okay. Could reduce speedo further for ≤560 width. Add within landscape block:
```
@media (pointer: coarse) and (max-height: 520px) and (max-width: 560px) {
  .speedo { width: 142px; height: 84px; }
  ...
  .touch-controls button {width:52;height:52}
}
```
Maybe unnecessary.

Let's apply.

